            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.071,
                0.258,
                0.4,
                0.307
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.13: (a) Streaks of pink colour spreading out; (b) Uniform pink colour in glass tumbler"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.083,
            0.884,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Initially, you will see some streaks of pink colour spreading out from the grain (Fig. 7.13a)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.14,
            0.884,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z With the passage of time, the entire bulk of water will acquire a uniform pink colour (Fig. 7.13b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.197,
            0.776,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Do you know why this happens?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.216,
            0.883,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This happens because the water particles are in constant motion. First they pull out the particles of potassium permanganate from its grain, and later they hit these particles so that they get spread throughout the liquid. In the case of many substances, the constituent particles"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.326,
            0.883,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "are held together strongly that the water particles are unable to pull these out. Such substances, like sand, are insoluble in water."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.375,
            0.49,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think like a scientist"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.409,
            0.387,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try it yourself!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.426,
            0.579,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take three clean glass tumblers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.446,
            0.861,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pour hot water in one of them, water at room temperature in the second and ice-cold water in the third."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.482,
            0.852,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Drop a small grain of potassium permanganate into each of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.501,
            0.765,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Watch carefully and compare. What do you observe?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.565,
            0.247,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.162,
                0.565,
                0.247,
                0.657
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.523,
            0.862,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water particles move faster in hot water compared to water at room temperature, and even slower in ice-cold water. As a result, the potassium permanganate spreads the fastest in hot water, less quickly in water at room temperature, and the slowest in ice-cold water. Hence, the movement of particles increases when heat is provided."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.624,
            0.623,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try to depict it by "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "drawing",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " a diagram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.689,
            0.602,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How can we "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "demonstrate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the movement of gas particles that cannot be seen with the naked eye?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.612,
            0.669,
            0.797,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.612,
                0.669,
                0.797,
                0.785
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_17.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.27,
            0.81,
            0.627,
            0.834
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 7.9: Let us find out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.845,
            0.866,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Light an incense stick in one corner of the room (Fig. 7.14)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.868,
            0.654,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Wait for a few minutes and observe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.889,
            0.736,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Do you notice the fragrance from a distance?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
